#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_financial_data.rst:3
msgid "Insert financial data"
msgstr "Вставка финансовых данных"

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_financial_data.rst:5
msgid ""
"When building reports and dashboards, it may be useful to include certain "
"accounting-related data, such as account IDs, credits and debits for "
"specific accounts, and dates of the start and end of the tax year."
msgstr ""
"При создании отчётов и дашбордов может быть полезно включить определённые "
"бухгалтерские данные, такие как ID счетов, кредиты и дебеты для конкретных "
"счетов, а также даты начала и окончания налогового года."

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_financial_data.rst:9
msgid ""
":ref:`Odoo-specific spreadsheet functions <spreadsheet/functions/odoo>` "
"allow you to retrieve such accounting data from your database and insert it "
"into a spreadsheet."
msgstr ""
":ref:`Специфичные для Odoo функции электронных таблиц <spreadsheet/functions/"
"odoo>` позволяют извлекать такие бухгалтерские данные из вашей базы данных и "
"вставлять их в электронную таблицу."

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:3
msgid "Insert a list"
msgstr "Вставка списка"

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:5
msgid "There are two ways to insert an Odoo list into an Odoo spreadsheet:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:7
msgid ""
":ref:`Insert a list from an Odoo list view <spreadsheet/insert-list/from-"
"view>` into an Odoo spreadsheet, Odoo dashboard, or quote calculator "
"spreadsheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:10
msgid ""
":ref:`Insert a list that retrieves Odoo data directly from an Odoo "
"spreadsheet <spreadsheet/insert-list/from-spreadsheet>`. This option allows "
"data to be pulled from any model, including models for which no list view is "
"available, e.g., the *Sales Order Line* model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:14
msgid ""
"In both cases, the list is connected to the underlying database data thanks "
"to its unique :ref:`data source <spreadsheet/insert/data-sources>`, which "
"keeps the data up-to-date and provides :ref:`access to the underlying data "
"<spreadsheet/insert/accessing-data>` directly from the spreadsheet. However, "
"whether or not the list expands to accommodate new records depends on "
"whether it is a :ref:`static or dynamic list <spreadsheet/insert-list/static-"
"vs-dynamic>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:23
msgid "Static vs dynamic lists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:25
msgid ""
"When a list from an Odoo list view is inserted into an Odoo spreadsheet, it "
"is, by default, a *static* list, where each cell retrieves data from the "
"database via an :ref:`Odoo-specific function <spreadsheet/insert-list/static-"
"functions>`. The list's data is kept up to date, but it does not expand to "
"accommodate new records."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:30
msgid ""
"Inserting an Odoo list directly from an Odoo spreadsheet results in a "
"*dynamic* list, where a single :ref:`Odoo-specific array function "
"<spreadsheet/insert-list/dynamic-function>` retrieves data from the "
"database. The list's data is kept up to date and, if desired, the array "
"function :ref:`can be modified <spreadsheet/insert-list/dynamic-all-"
"records>` to allow the list to expand to accommodate new records."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:37
msgid ""
"A static list can be :ref:`converted to a dynamic list <spreadsheet/insert-"
"list/static-convert>` and a dynamic list can be :ref:`converted to a static "
"list <spreadsheet/insert-list/dynamic-convert>` if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:44
msgid "Insert an Odoo list from a list view"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:47
msgid ""
"Before inserting a list into a spreadsheet, consider which fields should be "
"visible as well as how the records are filtered and/or sorted. This can "
"impact both the loading time and the user-friendliness of the spreadsheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:50
msgid ""
":doc:`Property fields <../../../essentials/property_fields>` visible in a "
"list view are included when the list is inserted into a spreadsheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:53
msgid ""
"To insert a list from an :ref:`Odoo list view <studio/views/multiple-records/"
"list>` into an Odoo spreadsheet:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:56
msgid ""
"With the relevant list view open, click the :icon:`fa-"
"cog` :guilabel:`(Actions)` icon beside the name of the view, "
"then :menuselection:`Spreadsheet -->` :icon:`oi-view-"
"list` :menuselection:`Insert list in spreadsheet`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:61
msgid ""
"To insert only specific records, select the relevant records, click "
"the :icon:`fa-cog` :guilabel:`Actions` button that appears at the top center "
"of the screen, then :icon:`oi-view-list` :guilabel:`Insert in spreadsheet`."
msgstr ""
"Чтобы вставить только определенные записи, выберите нужные записи, нажмите "
"кнопку :icon:`fa-cog` :guilabel:`Действия`, которая появляется вверху по "
"центру экрана, затем :icon:`oi-view-list` :guilabel:`Вставить в электронную "
"таблицу`."

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:65
msgid "In the window that opens, edit the :guilabel:`List name` if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:67
msgid ""
"Edit the number of :guilabel:`Records`, i.e., rows, to be inserted, if "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:69
msgid ""
"By default, the number shown is the number of records visible on the first "
"page of the list view. For example, if the list contains 150 records but "
"only 80 are visible, this field will show 80."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:73
msgid ""
"A list inserted from an Odoo list view is a :ref:`static list <spreadsheet/"
"insert-list/static-vs-dynamic>` that will not automatically expand to "
"accommodate new records. If it is likely that new records will be added in "
"the database, consider adding extra rows when inserting the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:78
msgid ""
"Click :guilabel:`Blank spreadsheet` to create a new spreadsheet, or select "
"in which existing spreadsheet the list should be inserted."
msgstr ""
"Нажмите :guilabel:`Пустая электронная таблица`, чтобы создать новую "
"электронную таблицу, или выберите, в какую существующую электронную таблицу "
"следует вставить список."

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:83
msgid ""
"The list is inserted into a new sheet in the spreadsheet. The sheet tab in "
"the bottom bar shows the name of the list followed by the list ID, e.g., "
"*Quotations by Total (List #1)*. A panel on the right side of the "
"spreadsheet shows the :ref:`list properties <spreadsheet/insert-list/"
"properties>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:87
msgid ""
"By default, the list is a :ref:`static list <spreadsheet/insert-list/static-"
"vs-dynamic>`, where each cell contains an :ref:`Odoo-specific function "
"<spreadsheet/insert-list/static-functions>` that retrieves data from the "
"database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:92
msgid ""
"The :guilabel:`List name` is used in the sheet name and in the :ref:`list "
"properties <spreadsheet/insert-list/properties>`, and can be edited at any "
"time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:94
msgid ""
"Records/rows can also be :ref:`added manually <spreadsheet/insert-list/"
"static-add-records>` after the spreadsheet has been inserted. Alternatively, "
"the inserted list can be :ref:`converted to a dynamic list <spreadsheet/"
"insert-list/static-convert>` to allow it to expand to accommodate new "
"records."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:98
msgid ""
"When inserting a list into a new spreadsheet, the spreadsheet is saved in "
"the **Odoo Documents** app in the :icon:`fa-hdd-o` :guilabel:`My Drive` "
"personal folder."
msgstr ""
"При вставке списка в новую электронную таблицу она сохраняется в приложении "
"**Odoo Документы** в :icon:`fa-hdd-o` :guilabel:`Мой диск` личной папке."

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:100
msgid ""
"To sever the link between an inserted list and the database, select the "
"entire list, right-click and select :icon:`fa-clipboard` :guilabel:`Copy`, "
"then right-click again and select :menuselection:`Paste special --> Paste as "
"value`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:107
msgid "Static list functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:109
msgid ""
"A static list uses the following :ref:`Odoo-specific functions <spreadsheet/"
"functions/odoo>` to retrieve the header and field values, respectively, via "
"its :ref:`data source <spreadsheet/insert/data-sources>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:118
#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:223
msgid "The arguments of the function are as follows:"
msgstr "Аргументы функции следующие:"

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:120
msgid ""
"`list_id`: the ID assigned when the list is inserted. The first list "
"inserted into a spreadsheet is assigned list ID `1`, the second, list ID "
"`2`, etc."
msgstr ""
"`list_id`: идентификатор, присваиваемый при вставке списка. Первому списку, "
"вставленному в электронную таблицу, присваивается идентификатор списка `1`, "
"второму — идентификатор списка `2` и т. д."

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:122
msgid ""
"`index`: identifies the line on which the record appeared in the list before "
"insertion. The first line has an index of `1`, the second an index of `2`, "
"etc."
msgstr ""
"`index`: определяет строку, в которой запись отображалась в списке перед "
"вставкой. Первая строка имеет индекс `1`, вторая — индекс `2` и т. д."

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:124
msgid "`field_name`: the technical name of the field."
msgstr "`field_name`: техническое название поля."

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:127
msgid ""
"Clicking on an individual cell displays the related formula, if relevant, in "
"the formula bar. To display all the formulas of a spreadsheet at the same "
"time, click :menuselection:`View -->` :icon:`fa-eye` :menuselection:`Show --"
"> Formulas` on the menu bar. The example below shows the functions used to "
"retrieve list headers and values."
msgstr ""
"При нажатии на отдельную ячейку в строке формул отображается связанная "
"формула, если она есть. Чтобы одновременно отобразить все формулы "
"электронной таблицы, нажмите :menuselection:`Вид -->` :icon:`fa-"
"eye` :menuselection:`Показать --> Формулы` в строке меню. В приведенном ниже "
"примере показаны функции, используемые для извлечения заголовков и значений "
"списка."

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:132
msgid "Viewing formulas of spreadsheet cells"
msgstr "Просмотр формул ячеек электронной таблицы"

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:138
msgid "Convert a static list to a dynamic list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:140
msgid ""
"To allow an inserted list to expand and accommodate new records, convert the "
"list to a :ref:`dynamic list <spreadsheet/insert-list/static-vs-dynamic>`, "
"then :ref:`update the array function <spreadsheet/insert-list/dynamic-all-"
"records>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:144
msgid "There are two main ways to convert a static list to a dynamic list:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:146
msgid ""
":ref:`Duplicate the list from the list properties <spreadsheet/insert-list/"
"duplicate>`. The new dynamic list has the same styling as the original list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:150
msgid ""
"With this method, the new dynamic list is assigned the next available list "
"ID. This means multiple lists can be associated with the same model, but "
"have distinct configurations or calculations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:154
msgid ""
"**Re-insert a dynamic list from the Data menu.** On the sheet that contains "
"the static list, position the cursor in an empty cell. "
"Click :menuselection:`Data -->` :icon:`os-insert-list` :menuselection:`Re-"
"insert dynamic list` from the menu bar, then select the relevant list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:159
msgid "A new dynamic list appears, with the same styling as the original list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:162
msgid ""
"It is also possible to re-insert a dynamic list by entering "
"the :ref:`function of the dynamic list <spreadsheet/insert-list/dynamic-"
"function>` in an empty cell, e.g., `=ODOO.LIST(1)`, where `1` is "
"the :ref:`list ID <spreadsheet/insert-list/properties-id>`. However, with "
"this method, the table styling needs to be re-applied manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:168
msgid ""
"When a dynamic list is re-inserted from the data menu or by manually "
"entering the dynamic list function, the static and dynamic lists share the "
"same data source and, consequently, the same list ID. To avoid confusion, "
"delete the original static list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:172
msgid ""
"The top-left cell of the new dynamic list contains an :ref:`Odoo-specific "
"array function <spreadsheet/insert-list/dynamic-function>` that retrieves "
"data from the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:176
#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:230
msgid ""
":ref:`Determine the number of records displayed in a dynamic list "
"<spreadsheet/insert-list/dynamic-all-records>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:182
msgid "Insert an Odoo list from a spreadsheet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/productivity/spreadsheet/insert/insert_list.rst:184
msgid "To insert an Odoo list directly from an Odoo spreadsheet:"
